<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-14294] .NET: ClientServerCompatibilityTest is flaky</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14294</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;ClientServerCompatibilityTest fails for two reasons:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. &lt;tt&gt;Failed to establish Ignite thin client connection, examine inner exceptions for details. (Connection refused 127.0.0.1:10892)&lt;/tt&gt; - check process output, is there a different port used for the client connector?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. &lt;tt&gt;GridUnsafe cannot access class jdk.internal.misc.SharedSecrets&lt;/tt&gt; - we should pass &lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;add-exports&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-illegal-access=permit&lt;/tt&gt; JVM options when running on Java9+, see &lt;tt&gt;Jvm.IsJava9&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
